OUT|h2|
OUT|h2|
OUT|h2|install [flags] <module> [<version>]
OUT|h2|    ? Description: Installs a module available in a configured repository.
OUT|h2|
OUT|h2|    ? Arguments
OUT|h2|        ? module: Name of module to install
OUT|h2|        ? version: Version (or version expression) of module to install; defaults to the latest available if unspecified.
OUT|h2|
OUT|h2|    ? Flags:
OUT|h2|        ? -env, -e <value> : Semicolon separated paths to the environment files in json format. See wiki for details.
OUT|h2|        ? -latest, -l : Installs the latest available version of this module without prompting the user.
OUT|h2|        ? -prompt, -p : Prompts user which version to install, if more then one found.
OUT|h2|        ? -dev : Sets the DeveloperMode flag for the module's lifecycle. Key consequences of this are that ^Sources will be configured for resources in the module, and installer methods will be called with the dev mode flag set. In addition, transactions will not be rolled back if installation fails.
OUT|h2|        ? -quiet, -q : Produces minimal output from the command.
OUT|h2|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output from the command.
OUT|h2|        ? -keywords, -k <value> : Searches for modules matching some set of keywords.
OUT|h2|        ? -bypass-py-deps : Skip installing python dependencies
OUT|h2|        ? -extra-pip-flags <value> : Extra flags to pass to pip when installing python dependencies. Surround the flags (and values) with quotes if spaces are present. Default flags are "--target <target> --python-version <pyversion> --only-binary=:all:".
OUT|h2|        ? -synchronous : DEPRECATED. Dependencies are now always loaded synchronously with independent lifecycle phases doing their own multi-threading as needed.
OUT|h2|        ? -force, -f : Allows the user to install a newer version of an existing module without running update steps.
OUT|h2|        ? -create-lockfile, -lock : Upon install, creates/updates the module's lock file.
OUT|h2|        ? -skip-sync : In developer mode, skips recording the file hashes that sync uses to detect changes. The next sync of the module records them instead.
OUT|h2|
OUT|h2|    ? Examples
OUT|h2|        ?     install HS.JSON 1.x        
OUT|h2|            Installs the most recent 1.x version of HS.JSON available in any configured repository in the current namespace.
OUT|h2|        ?     install registry/HS.JSON        
OUT|h2|            Installs the most recent version of HS.JSON from the `registry` repository.
OUT|h2|        ?     install -bypass-py-deps HS.JSON        
OUT|h2|            Installs HS.JSON without installing python dependencies
OUT|h2|        ?     install -extra-pip-flags "--timeout 30" HS.JSON        
OUT|h2|            Installs HS.JSON but set pip timeout to 30 seconds
OUT|h2|        ? install -env /path/to/env1.json;/path/to/env2.json example-package        
OUT|h2|            Installs example-package using the /path/to/env1.json and /path/to/env2.json as the install time configuration
