OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|arrange [flags] [<module>]
OUT|h7|    ? Description:     Rearranges the resources in a module manifest to follow the standard format.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? module: Name of module to rearrange
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -all : If specified, rearrange all modules loaded in development mode (rather than just the current one).
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|compile [flags] <module>
OUT|h7|    ? Description: This command is an alias for `module-action module-name compile`
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? module: Name of module on which to perform compile action
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -env, -e <value> : Semicolon separated paths to the environment files in json format. See wiki for details.
OUT|h7|        ? -only, -o : Only runs the specified phase(s), rather than also running predecessors.
OUT|h7|        ? -dev : Sets the DeveloperMode flag for the module's lifecycle. Key consequences of this are that ^Sources will be configured for resources in the module, and installer methods will be called with the dev mode flag set.
OUT|h7|        ? -quiet, -q : Produces minimal output. For test and verify: suppresses build/install noise while still showing the result summary and any failures.
OUT|h7|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output. For test and verify: shows per-method results in the result summary when combined with -f; without -f only the summary is shown.
OUT|h7|        ? -format, -f <json/yaml/toon> : (test and verify only) One-shot output format override for the test result summary. Overrides the persistent default set via 'config set TestReportFormat <format>'. When neither -f nor config is set, the default summary and legacy failure lines are shown. Use 'config delete TestReportFormat' to revert to default.
OUT|h7|        ? -output-file <value> : (test and verify only) Path to write full test results to a file. Format is inferred from the file extension (.json, .yaml, .toon, .xml).
OUT|h7|        ? -export-deps <0/1> : If specified, controls whether dependencies are exported. If omitted, defaults to the value of the #EXPORTDEPENDENCIES in lifecycle class. This modifier is only used in "Package" and "Publish" lifecycles.
OUT|h7|        ? -skip-sync : In developer mode, skips recording the file hashes that sync uses to detect changes during the compile phase. The next sync of the module records them instead.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|config <action> [<key> [<value>]]
OUT|h7|    ? Description: Update ZPM settings. Setting is a key-value pair.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? action: One of settings actions: list, get, set, delete
OUT|h7|        ? key: Setting key
OUT|h7|        ? value: Setting value
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ? config set analytics 0        
OUT|h7|            Disable collecting analytics data
OUT|h7|        ? config set analytics 1        
OUT|h7|            Enable collecting analytics data
OUT|h7|        ? config list        
OUT|h7|            list all settings
OUT|h7|        ? config get analytics        
OUT|h7|            get value for analytics key
OUT|h7|        ? config delete analytics        
OUT|h7|            reset to default value for analytics key
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|default-modifiers [flags]
OUT|h7|    ? Description:     Manages default modifiers to use for all package manager commands in the current namespace.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -set : Set the default modifiers to the provided modifiers. Note: this just appends to existing modifiers. DOES NOT delete any defaults.
OUT|h7|        ? -get : Prints the default modifiers to the current device.
OUT|h7|        ? -delete : Deletes all registered default modifiers.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?     default-modifiers -set -DNoTransaction=1 -DUpdateSnapshots=1        
OUT|h7|            Set custom modifiers -DNoTransaction=1 and -DUpdateSnapshots=1 with every package manager command
OUT|h7|        ?     default-modifiers -get        
OUT|h7|            Get currently set custom modifiers.
OUT|h7|        ?     default-modifiers -delete        
OUT|h7|            Delete currently set custom modifiers.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|dependency-analyzer [flags] <moduleOrItem>
OUT|h7|    ? Alias: deps
OUT|h7|    ? Description:         For a module, inspects all items in the provided module and checks for invalid references to items
OUT|h7|        that are not in the module and not in any of the module's dependencies.
OUT|h7|        For an item, finds all its references to other items, or optionally list
OUT|h7|        just the invalid references of the item as well.
OUT|h7|        Dependency analyzer supports .cls and .inc items. Other item types are not yet supported.
OUT|h7|        The references are written to the current device.
OUT|h7|    
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? moduleOrItem: Name of module / item to inspect
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -invalid-only <value> : Will only be applied when the input is an item name. Default to 1, i.e default to show invalid references only. If specified to 0, will show all references to the item.
OUT|h7|        ? -ignore-str <value> : If specified, ignore specific string references provided as a comma-separated string, including class names
OUT|h7|        ? -ignore-str-all : If specified, ignore all string references, including class names
OUT|h7|        ? -direct-deps-only : If specified, flag references based on direct dependencies only instead of allowing for transitive dependencies
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?         deps MyModuleName -ignore-str MyClassName1,MyClassName2
OUT|h7|            
OUT|h7|            Runs the dependency analyzer on the module MyModuleName to find invalid references, and ignore string references MyClassName1 and MyClassName2.
OUT|h7|        ?         deps MyClassName3.cls -invalid-only 0 -ignore-str-all
OUT|h7|            
OUT|h7|            Runs the dependency analyzer on item MyClassName3.cls to find all its references, and ignore all string references.
OUT|h7|        ?         deps MyIncludeName.inc
OUT|h7|            
OUT|h7|            Runs the dependency analyzer on item MyIncludeName.inc to find all invalid references in it.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|enable [flags]
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -version, -v <value> : A special version of IPM can be provided. If not specified, the latest version from the registry will be installed (hence is not required if quiet flag is set).
OUT|h7|        ? -namespaces, -ns <value> : Comma-separated namespaces in which IPM needs to be enabled.
OUT|h7|        ? -globally, -g : Will install IPM in all explicit namespaces that currently do not have IPM installed. Unless using it together with the -map option, will not include %SYS. By default, this modifier is not set and will not install globally.
OUT|h7|        ? -local-only : If specified, only local artifacts will be used for installation. By default, this modifier is not set and will not limit to local artifacts.
OUT|h7|        ? -allow-upgrade : If specified, will also check for IPM version in specified namespaces and upgrade if version is lower than the target version. By default, this modifier is not ste and will not allow upgrade.
OUT|h7|        ? -map, -m : If specified, will map IPM code from the current namespace-default code database rather than installing a separate copy.
OUT|h7|        ? -repos, -r : If specified, will map repository settings across namespaces. Must be used together with -map.
OUT|h7|        ? -remote <value> : If specified, will use fetch IPM versions from this remote repository. If this is omitted and multiple remote repositories are present, an error will occur.
OUT|h7|        ? -quiet, -q : Quiet mode. By default, this modifier is not set and will display the contents onto the terminal/caller command line.
OUT|h7|        ? -preview, -p : Preview what will be changed without actually making the changes.
OUT|h7|        ? -community : If specified, will reset repository to the community repository and map IPM to all namespaces along with the repository settings. This is functionaly equivalent to "repo -delete-all", "repo -reset-defaults", and "enable -map -repos -globally". With this modifier, all other modifiers will be ignored.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -map -globally
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            Make IPM available in all namespaces (including %SYS) by mapping the version in the current namespace default routine database. Namespace-specific installation will override this.
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -v 0.3.4 -q -ns NS1,NS2,NS3 -remote registry
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            Install IPM version 0.3.4 from the remote registry namd "registry" in quiet mode in namespaces: NS1, NS2, NS3.
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -globally
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            Install IPM in all non-%SYS explicit namespaces, and select version later in terminal prompt menu. This works if there is only 1 remote repository configured.
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -v latest -globally
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            User wants to get the latest version of IPM from the registry server, and install it in all non-%SYS explicit namespaces. This works if there is only 1 remote repository configured.
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -v latest -allow-upgrade NS1,NS2,NS3
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            Install or upgrade IPM to latest IPM version in namespaces: NS1, NS2, NS3. This works if there is only 1 remote repository configured.
OUT|h7|        ?             enable -community
OUT|h7|                
OUT|h7|            Reset repository to the community repository and map IPM to all namespaces along with the repository settings.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
