OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|history [flags] [<action> [<argument>]]
OUT|h7|    ? Alias: log
OUT|h7|    ? Description: Manage history of package installation/uninstallation. Commands logged are install, load, uninstall, and update. By default, all entries will be affected. To specify filters, use the -Dcol=val syntax. See examples for more.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? action: One of history actions: find (default), details, delete, schema
OUT|h7|        ? argument: Argument for `details` command
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -globally, -g : If specified, will affect all namespaces instead of the current one. Defaults to false.
OUT|h7|        ? -sort, -asc <value> : List the history logs in a specific order. Allowed values are asc and desc. Default behaviour is to list logs in descending order of %ID.
OUT|h7|        ? -limit <value> : If specified, will only list the specified number of logs. If set to 0, all logs will be displayed. If omitted, will use the value returned by `zpm "config get DefaultLogEntryLimit"`.
OUT|h7|        ? -showPhases, -p, -phases : Show lifecycle phase information in details view.
OUT|h7|        ? -confirm : If present, will delete all records in the current namespace. Ignored if -globally is passed too.
OUT|h7|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output from the command.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ? history find         
OUT|h7|            Show history of all packages in the current namespace in descending order
OUT|h7|        ? history find -DCommandString="load*"        
OUT|h7|            Show history of all packages in the current namespace where command starts with "load"
OUT|h7|        ? history find -DCommitted=1        
OUT|h7|            Show history of all packages in the current namespace where the command has been committed `to disk`. Committed is not the same as successful, because a failed action can keep changes, for example in dev mode or without a transaction.
OUT|h7|        ? history find -DSucess="0*"        
OUT|h7|            Show history of all packages in the current namespace where the command has errored
OUT|h7|        ? history find -DTimeStart=">2000-01-01 00:00:00"        
OUT|h7|            Show history of all packages in the current namespace where start time is later than 2000-01-01 00:00:00
OUT|h7|        ? history find -sort asc -limit 5        
OUT|h7|            Show 5 history records in the current namespace in ascending order
OUT|h7|        ? history schema        
OUT|h7|            Show column names that the table can be filtered by
OUT|h7|        ? history find -Daction=install -Dpackage=zpip        
OUT|h7|            Show only installation history of package "zpip" in the current namespace 
OUT|h7|        ? history find -globally -Daction=install -Dpackage=zpip        
OUT|h7|            Show only installation history of package "zpip" in all namespaces 
OUT|h7|        ? history delete -confirm        
OUT|h7|            Delete all histories in the namespace
OUT|h7|        ? history details 3 -phases        
OUT|h7|            Show details of history item with ID 3 and information for each undergone lifecyle phase
OUT|h7|        ? config set HistoryRetain "days"         
OUT|h7|            Enable history auto-purge. Example: config set HistoryRetain 30.
OUT|h7|        ? config set HistoryRetain 0        
OUT|h7|            Disable history auto-purge
OUT|h7|        ? config get HistoryRetain        
OUT|h7|            Display the current history retention setting.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|import [flags] <source>
OUT|h7|    ? Description: Imports classes from a file or file(s), reexporting to source control if needed.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? source: File or directory to import
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -quiet, -q : Produces minimal output from the command.
OUT|h7|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output from the command.
OUT|h7|        ? -norecurse : If importing a directory, do not recurse (default is to load directories recursively)
OUT|h7|        ? -nocompile : Skip compiling imported classes (default is to compile them)
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?     import C:\Temp\MyExport.xml        
OUT|h7|            Import and compile the class or classes from the given file
OUT|h7|        ?     import C:\Temp\MyFlatExportDir\ -norecurse -nocompile        
OUT|h7|            Import the classes from the given directory, located at its root level only. Classes are loaded but not compiled.
OUT|h7|
