OUT|h7|uninstall [flags] [<module>]
OUT|h7|    ? Description:     Uninstalls a module currently installed locally. This will be prevented if other modules
OUT|h7|    depend on the named module, unless the -force flag is specified.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Arguments
OUT|h7|        ? module: Name of module to uninstall
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -all, -a : Uninstalls all modules installed in the current namespace.
OUT|h7|        ? -global, -g : Also uninstalls modules with 'global scope' (available in all namespaces); by default, these are skipped.
OUT|h7|        ? -force, -f : If specified, the module will be uninstalled even if other modules depend on it.
OUT|h7|        ? -recurse, -r : Also recursively uninstall dependencies. By default, will not uninstall dependencies that are also required by other installed modules; the -force flag overrides this.
OUT|h7|        ? -quiet, -q : Produces minimal output from the command.
OUT|h7|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output from the command.
OUT|h7|        ? -purge : Purge data from tables during uninstall.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?     uninstall HS.JSON        
OUT|h7|            Uninstalls HS.JSON from the current namespace.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|unmap [flags]
OUT|h7|    ? Description:         Unmap %IPM package and routines in specified namespaces. Will Skip non-mapped namespaces.
OUT|h7|        If repository settings are mapped, will also unmap repository settings.
OUT|h7|    
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Flags:
OUT|h7|        ? -namespaces, -ns <value> : Comma-separated namespaces in which IPM mapping needs to be deleted.
OUT|h7|        ? -globally, -g : Will unmap IPM in all explicit namespaces that currently do not have IPM installed.
OUT|h7|        ? -quiet, -q : Quiet mode. By default, this modifier is not set and will display the contents onto the terminal/caller command line.
OUT|h7|        ? -repos-only : If specified, will only unmap repository settings across namespaces. This doesn't affect mapping of IPM packages and routines.
OUT|h7|
OUT|h7|    ? Examples
OUT|h7|        ?         unmap -ns NS1,NS2,NS3
OUT|h7|            
OUT|h7|            Unmap IPM from namespaces NS1, NS2, NS3.
OUT|h7|        ?         unmap -g
OUT|h7|            
OUT|h7|            Unmap IPM from all namespaces
