OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|module-action <module> <actions> [flags]
OUT|h9|    ? Description: Performs operations on modules - compiling, running tests, packaging/registering, etc.
OUT|h9|You can use this by starting a command with the module name.
OUT|h9|Note that flags appear *after* all actions.
OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|The standard lifecycle phases are:
OUT|h9|* clean: removes all dependencies that are not required by other installed modules and
OUT|h9|their resources. Dependencies required by other modules will also be removed if the -DClean.Force=1 flag is specified.
OUT|h9|* reload: pulls module source code into the namespace from disk. Does not compile.
OUT|h9|* validate: ensures that module resource processor attributes are valid, and that the
OUT|h9|resources exported to the filesystem (and possible to source control) are consistent
OUT|h9|with what is in the database.
OUT|h9|* compile: compiles all resources within the module.
OUT|h9|* activate: performs post-compilation installation/configuration steps.
OUT|h9|* makedeployed: deploys resources within the module for which deployment is enabled.
OUT|h9|* document: regenerates the API documentation for the module
OUT|h9|* test: runs any unit tests associated with the module, in the current namespace.
OUT|h9|* package: exports the module's resources and bundles them into a module artifact (.tgz file).
OUT|h9|* verify: installs that artifact in a separate namespace, then runs integration tests (if any).
OUT|h9|* register: saves that artifact into the current namespace's module cache.
OUT|h9|This is accessible to other instances configured to look at the current namespace as a
OUT|h9|module repository.
OUT|h9|* publish: saves that artifact to the repository for which deployment is enabled.
OUT|h9|Currently, there may only be one of these per namespace.
OUT|h9|* applyupdatesteps: run any update steps for the module to become updated to the latest available version.
OUT|h9|Can also specify desired version to update to.
OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|    ? Arguments
OUT|h9|        ? module: Name of module on which to perform lifecycle actions
OUT|h9|        ? actions: Space-delimited list of module lifecycle phases to run
OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|    ? Flags:
OUT|h9|        ? -env, -e <value> : Semicolon separated paths to the environment files in json format. See wiki for details.
OUT|h9|        ? -only, -o : Only runs the specified phase(s), rather than also running predecessors.
OUT|h9|        ? -dev : Sets the DeveloperMode flag for the module's lifecycle. Key consequences of this are that ^Sources will be configured for resources in the module, and installer methods will be called with the dev mode flag set.
OUT|h9|        ? -quiet, -q : Produces minimal output. For test and verify: suppresses build/install noise while still showing the result summary and any failures.
OUT|h9|        ? -verbose, -v : Produces verbose output. For test and verify: shows per-method results in the result summary when combined with -f; without -f only the summary is shown.
OUT|h9|        ? -format, -f <json/yaml/toon> : (test and verify only) One-shot output format override for the test result summary. Overrides the persistent default set via 'config set TestReportFormat <format>'. When neither -f nor config is set, the default summary and legacy failure lines are shown. Use 'config delete TestReportFormat' to revert to default.
OUT|h9|        ? -output-file <value> : (test and verify only) Path to write full test results to a file. Format is inferred from the file extension (.json, .yaml, .toon, .xml).
OUT|h9|        ? -export-deps <0/1> : If specified, controls whether dependencies are exported. If omitted, defaults to the value of the #EXPORTDEPENDENCIES in lifecycle class. This modifier is only used in "Package" and "Publish" lifecycles.
OUT|h9|        ? -skip-sync : In developer mode, skips recording the file hashes that sync uses to detect changes during the compile phase. The next sync of the module records them instead.
OUT|h9|        ? -path, -p <value> : the specified path to export package.
OUT|h9|        ? -export-python-deps : If specified, exports Python dependencies. If omitted, defaults to false.
OUT|h9|        ? -include-tests : If specified, includes test-scoped resources in the package.
OUT|h9|        ? -repo, -r : Namespace-unique name of repository for the module to publish to (if deployment is enabled)
OUT|h9|        ? -use-external-name, -use-ext : Publish the package under the <ExternalName> of the package. If ExternalName is unspecified or illegal, an error will be thrown.
OUT|h9|        ? -recurse, -r : Runs the specified phase (makedeployed) on the module and all of its dependencies.
OUT|h9|
OUT|h9|    ? Examples
OUT|h9|        ? module-action MyModuleName compile        
OUT|h9|            Compiles the module named "MyModuleName"
OUT|h9|        ? MyModuleName clean register        
OUT|h9|            Performs multiple actions on the module named "MyModuleName"; "clean" deletes all of its dependenices, and "install" will then re-download them, package the module, and register it in the current namespace's module cache.
OUT|h9|        ? MyUIModule compile -v -DUIFW.force=42        
OUT|h9|            Compiles the module named MyUIModule with verbose output and pParams("UIFW","force") (passed to all lifecycle phases) set to 42.
OUT|h9|        ? MyModule verify -env /path/to/env.json        
OUT|h9|            Verify the module MyModule with the env file /path/to/env.json. The module is responsible for accessing the data using %IPM.General.EnvironmentConfig:GetArg()
